{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "One entry per Fact in model/deal.py (FIELD_REFERENCE.generated.md); tests/deals/test_fact_sheet.py fails if a Fact is not covered.",
    "Paths use the citation grammar with [*] for any key of a keyed collection; a fixed key (values_by_basis[as_is]) is listed before the [*] pattern, which then covers the remaining keys.",
    "kind subtree: every present fact under the path, labelled from its path (additional valuations and firm comparables keep the valuation shape).",
    "core: the judgement that a field is part of what its block must carry (true, or the deal types it is core for). A field is REQUIRED for a deal only when it is core for that deal type AND its block is fed by a non-optional slot for that type (docs/specs/slot-taxonomy model_block). required and expected_from are derived at read time from the taxonomy, never stored here.",
    "collection_label: the plural label of a required keyed collection shown once as missing when it has no entries.",
    "type_scoped_blocks: blocks a slot feeds only for some deal types even though the slot applies to all (the title search carries registered OC titles only on residual stock)."
  ],
  "type_scoped_blocks": {
    "oc_titles": [
      "residual_stock"
    ]
  },
